#TOPIC 2 - SETS IN PYTHON:

# SETS are collection of Unordered items.. har element of a set must be unique ,and immutable too.. mtlb int, float,tuple, boolean etc etc store kar skte hai'n..but list and dictionary nhi, as they're mutable

#dhyan dena, ke SET mutable hote hai (mtlb elemtn add ya remove kia ja skta hai)... pr set k andar ke elements IMMUTABLE hote hain... mtlb can't be changed

collection ={1 , 2 ,3 ,4 ,3 ,4, "hello" , "world" , 3.14}

print(type(collection)) #'set'  ayega
print(collection)   #dhyan dena k printing ORDER me nhi hogi.. randomly hogi 
#also.. set' , duplicate values ko sirf ek baar print krta hai

print(len(collection)) #ye bhi duplicate items ko sirf ek baar lega


null_set={} #ye empty set nhi hai, empty dictionary hai, 
empty_set= set() #YE HAI EMPTY SET

print(type(empty_set))


#METHODS OF SET:

#(1) - ADD method: adds an element to the set  ... as elements immutable hote hai, tuple daal skte hai'n pr list ya dictionary nhii - let's say agr list daali to error ayega "UN-HASHABLE TYPE: LIST".. cuz hash values(we know) change ho skti list ki ..

collection.add(45) 
collection.add("name")
collection.add(("yo" , "hey" , "wow"))  #ek poora TUPLE add krrhe hai'n
#agr duplicate values add kroge to bhi ek hi baar print hoga as we know

print(collection)

#(2)  - REMOVE:

collection.remove(4) #does'nt matter if value repeated hai.. sari uda dega
collection.remove(45)
print(collection)


#(3)  - CLEAR: empties the set

print(len(collection))

collection.clear()
print("new length is: " ,len(collection))

#(4)  - POP: gets a random value

collection={1, 2, 4, "hey", "yo", 663}

print(collection.pop())
print(collection.pop())

#(5) - UNION - jo join 2 sets just as in maths - output ek set ayega

collection2={23, 45, 56, 78, 4}

collection.union(collection2)

print(collection.union(collection2))

#(6) - INTERSECTION : iska bhi output ek set ayega

print(collection.intersection(collection2))




